From: Shijin Zhang <75300765+Dovis01@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 05:39:11 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 21/25] [Bugfix][Frontend] Force reasoning mode for GLM-5.3
 chat templates

GLM-5.3 keeps the GLM-4.x prompt and tool-call format but replaces the
enable_thinking switch with an always-on "Reasoning Effort:" header, so
its generation prompt always opens <think>. A request that passes
enable_thinking=false (or thinking=false) still gets a reasoning block,
but glm47_moe then stops parsing <think> and the reasoning lands in
content.

When the tokenizer's chat template is a GLM-5.3 template (GLM prompt and
tool markup, "Reasoning Effort:", no enable_thinking), ignore the switch
and keep reasoning extraction on. This also covers serving with a custom
--chat-template that maps thinking off to a low reasoning effort, as the
Kindling recipe does: detection reads the checkpoint's template.

Source: vLLM main d95d1dcfb, "[Bugfix][Frontend] Force reasoning mode
  for GLM-5.3 chat templates in the GLM MoE parser (#56994)", by Shijin
  Zhang with Chauncey; Apache-2.0. Backported without its tests
  (tests/reasoning/test_glm4_moe_reasoning_parser.py,
  test_anthropic_messages_conversion.py), which stay upstream.
  Supersedes kindlingai/glm-5.3-flash-gx10 @ c748079
  image/patches/glm53_reasoning_always_parsed.py (Matt Mastracci), which
  forced reasoning parsing for every template.
Upstream: merged on main as #56994 (2026-09-29), not in v0.31.0.
Claimed gain: correctness only; reasoning no longer leaks into content
  when a client turns thinking off.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
